<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">As mentioned in the text, any set with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> elements can be put in one-to-one correspondence with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  Consequently, any permutation of a set with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> elements can be obtained from a permutation of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and the correspondence.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1139" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">In Maple, we can use the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:subs" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">subs</Font></Hyperlink> command to transform a permutation of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> into a permutation of another set with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> elements.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1140" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">The <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:subs" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">subs</Font></Hyperlink> command is used to perform substitutions in an expression.  It has several forms, but we will use it with two arguments.  The second argument will be the permutation of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  The first argument will be a list of equations of the form <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> where <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> is an integer in <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> is the corresponding element of the set being permuted.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1141" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">For example, consider the set <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and the permutation <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  We establish the correspondence that 1, 2, and 3 are identified with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiYkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiY0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiY0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, respectively.  To produce the corresponding partition, we use the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:subs" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">subs</Font></Hyperlink> command with first argument <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> to specify the correspondence.  The second argument is the permutation <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1142" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs([1=&quot;a&quot;,2=&quot;b&quot;,3=&quot;c&quot;],[3,1,2]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NyVRImM2IlEiYUYkUSJiRiQ=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1144" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">As another example, consider the set <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and the permutation <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  Identify 1 with 2, 2 with 10, 3 with 13, and 4 with 19.  Then the following command produces the desired permutation.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1145" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs([1=2,2=10,3=13,4=19],[4,2,3,1]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NyYiIz4iIzUiIzgiIiM=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1147" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Note that <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:subs" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">subs</Font></Hyperlink> will allow you to list the equations without enclosing them in a list.  However, putting them in a list ensures that the substitutions are done simultaneously rather than sequentially.  In this example, sequential assignment would not have produced the correct result.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1150" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10"><Font italic="true">A procedure to apply permutations</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1151" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We conclude by writing a procedure that, given a set and a permutation of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> equal to the size of the set, will return the corresponding permutation of the set.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1152" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">The key is automating the creation of the equations defining the correspondence.  This can be done with the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:zip" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">zip</Font></Hyperlink> command.  Recall that <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:zip" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">zip</Font></Hyperlink> requires three arguments.  The second and third arguments are lists while the first argument is a procedure on two parameters.  The result is the list formed by applying the procedure to corresponding pairs of elements from the two lists.   </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1153" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We create a functional operator that takes two expressions and forms an equation from them.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1154" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">makeEqn := (a,b) -&gt; a=b;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">Zio2JEkiYUc2IkkiYkdGJUYlNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YlSSZhcnJvd0dGJUYlL0YkRiZGJUYlRiU=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L1155" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">makeEqn(5,a);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">LyIiJkkiYUc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1157" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Using the list <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and the list formed from the elements of the set <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> as the second and third arguments, <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:zip" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">zip</Font></Hyperlink> will produce the list of equations used in <Label label="L1142" view="label" executable="false"></Label>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1158" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">zip(makeEqn,[1,2,3],[&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;,&quot;c&quot;]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NyUvIiIiUSJhNiIvIiIjUSJiRiYvIiIkUSJjRiY=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1160" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">This is all we need to write a procedure that accepts a set and a permutation of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and returns the corresponding permutation of the elements of the set.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1161" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">permuteSet := proc(S::set,P::list(posint))
  local L, M, makeeqn, a, b, eqns;
  L := [op(S)];
  M := [$1..nops(S)];
  makeeqn := (a,b) -&gt; a=b;
  eqns := zip(makeeqn,M,L);
  return subs(eqns,P);
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1163" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Using the procedure, we can compute the permutation of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> corresponding to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1164" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">permuteSet({&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;,&quot;c&quot;,&quot;d&quot;,&quot;e&quot;},[3,5,2,1,4]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NydRImM2IlEiZUYkUSJiRiRRImFGJFEiZEYk</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Solutions to Computer Projects and Computations and Explorations</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="Heading 3" layout="Heading 3">Computer Projects 10</Text-field></Title><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1170" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10" leftmargin="10" spacebelow="10">Given positive integers <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, list all the <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>-combinations, with repetition allowed, of the set <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1171" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font italic="true">Solution:</Font> In Section 6.5 of this manual, we showed that the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:combinat,choose" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">choose</Font></Hyperlink> command could be used to generate combinations with repetition by repeating the elements in the list given as the first argument to <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:combinat,choose" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">choose</Font></Hyperlink>.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1172" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">To generate the 2-combinations of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, for example, we apply the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:combinat,choose" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">choose</Font></Hyperlink> command to the list consisting of 1, 2, and 3, each repeated twice.  Note that the number of repetitions must be the same as <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> in order to choose <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> all of the same object.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1173" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">choose([1$2, 2$2, 3$2],2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">Nyg3JCIiIkYkNyRGJCIiIzckRiQiIiQ3JEYmRiY3JEYmRig3JEYoRig=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1175" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Recall that <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">x$n</Font> generates the sequence of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>'s.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1177" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">The first argument to <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:combinat,choose" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">choose</Font></Hyperlink> can be generated using <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:seq" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">seq</Font></Hyperlink> as follows.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1178" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">[seq(i$2,i=1..3)];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NygiIiJGIyIiI0YkIiIkRiU=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1180" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We now write a procedure that accepts <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> as input and produces all <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEickYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>-combinations with repetition allowed.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1181" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">chooseRepetition := proc(n::posint, r::posint)
  local L, i;
  L := [seq(i$r,i=1..n)];
  return combinat[choose](L,r);
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1183" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We can obtain all of the 3-combinations of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> by</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1184" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">chooseRepetition(5,3);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output"></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="Heading 3" layout="Heading 3">Computations and Explorations 1</Text-field></Title><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1186" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10" leftmargin="10" spacebelow="10">Find the number of possible outcomes in a two-team playoff when the winner is the first team to win 5 out of 9, 6 out of 11, 7 out of 13, and 8 out of 15.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1188" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font italic="true">Solution:</Font> We will designate the two teams as 1 and 2 and model a playoff as a list of 1s and 2s.  For example, <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is a playoff in which team 1 wins the first game, team 2 wins games 2 and 3, team 1 wins games 4, 5, and 6, team 2 wins game 7, and them team 1 wins game 8.  If the winner is the first team to win 5 out of 9 games, then team 1 has won the tournament after 8 games.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1189" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We will write a procedure to produce all of the possible outcomes in a playoff where the winner is the first team to win <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> out of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> games.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1190" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">First we will create a small procedure that will determine, given a list of the outcomes of individual games and the number of games needed to win, whether a team has won the playoff or not.  The procedure will return true if one of the teams has won or false if neither team has reached the threshold for winning.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1191" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">The procedure counts the 1s and 2s in the list.  If either number is equal to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, it returns true. </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1192" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">playoffWon := proc(L::list({1,2}),n::posint)
  local n1, n2, i;
  n1 := 0;
  n2 := 0;
  for i from 1 to nops(L) do
    if L[i] = 1 then
      n1 := n1 + 1;
    else
      n2 := n2 + 1;
    end if;
  end do;
  if n1 = n or n2 = n then
    return true;
  else
    return false;
  end if;
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1194" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">For instance, in our example <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, the procedure recognizes that the playoff has been won.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1195" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">playoffWon([1,2,2,1,1,1,2,1],5);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">SSV0cnVlRyUqcHJvdGVjdGVkRw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1197" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We will construct the possible outcomes as follows.  Begin with a set <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">outcomes</Font> and a list <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">S</Font>.  Initialize <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">outcomes</Font> to the empty set and <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">S</Font> to the list <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1198" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Consider the first element of <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">S</Font>, say <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">p</Font>.  Remove <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">p</Font> from the list.  Then construct the two lists formed by adding 1 and 2 respectively to <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">p</Font>.  For each of these, use <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">playoffWon</Font> to determine whether or not they are outcomes.  If so, they are added to the <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">outcomes</Font> set, and if not, they are added to the end of <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">S</Font>.  When <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">S</Font> is empty, then <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">outcomes</Font> consists of all possible outcomes of the playoff.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1199" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Here is the procedure.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1200" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">allPlayoffs := proc(n::posint)
  local outcomes, S, p, p1, p2;
  outcomes := {};
  S := [[1],[2]];
  while S &lt;&gt; [] do
    p := S[1];
    S := S[2..-1];
    p1 := [op(p),1];
    p2 := [op(p),2];
    if playoffWon(p1,n) then
      outcomes := outcomes union {p1};
    else
      S := [op(S),p1];
    end if;
    if playoffWon(p2,n) then
      outcomes := outcomes union {p2};
    else
      S := [op(S),p2];
    end if;
  end do;
  return outcomes;
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1202" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We now apply this procedure to playoffs that are best 3 out of 5.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1203" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">best3of5 := allPlayoffs(3);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L1204" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">nops(best3of5);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">IiM/</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1206" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The reader is left to apply the procedure to the cases called for in the problem and to conjecture a general formula.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="Heading 3" layout="Heading 3">Computations and Explorations 3</Text-field></Title><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1207" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10" leftmargin="10" spacebelow="10">Verify that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is divisible by the square of a prime, when <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, 2, or 4, for as many positive integers <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> as you can.  [The theorem that tells that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is divisible by the square of a prime for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation><Font encoding="UTF-8">, 2, or 4 was proved in 1996 by Andrew Granville and Olivier Ramar\303\251.  Their proof settled a conjecture made in 1980 by Paul Erd\305\221s and Ron Graham.]</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1208" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font italic="true">Solution:</Font>  We will first consider one example to see exactly what we need to do.  Then we will write a general procedure.  Consider <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, the smallest <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> for which the theorem is true.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1222" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">First, compute <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1223" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">c := binomial(6,3);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">IiM/</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1225" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">To determine whether or not <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is divisible by the square of a prime, we'll look at its prime factorization.  If any of the exponents in the prime factorization are 2 or greater, then we know the number is divisible by the square of the corresponding prime.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1230" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We use the command <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:ifactors" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">ifactors</Font></Hyperlink> (first discussed in Section 4.3 of this manual).  The <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:ifactors" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">ifactors</Font></Hyperlink> command requires one argument, an integer.  It's output is a list of the form <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> where <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVElc2lnbkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVElc2lnbkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> is positive or negative 1; <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> are the primes in the prime factorization; and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> are the corresponding exponents.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1226" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Apply <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:ifactors" hyperlink="true"><Font executable="false" style="Maple Input" underline="true">ifactors</Font></Hyperlink> to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1227" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">ifactors(c);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NyQiIiI3JDckIiIjRiY3JCIiJkYj</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1231" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The result tells us that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1232" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We are interested in the exponents of the primes.  We take the second element of the list to obtain the list of pairs of primes and their exponents without the sign component.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1233" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">cFacts := ifactors(c)[2];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">NyQ3JCIiI0YkNyQiIiYiIiI=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1235" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">This gives us a list of lists, where the first element in each internal list is the prime factor and the second element in each pair is the exponent associated to that prime.  Since we are only interested in the exponents, we'll separate them out.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1236" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">cPowers := seq(x[2],x=cFacts);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">NiQiIiMiIiI=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1238" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Provided that there is an exponent of 2 or larger, we know that the square of a prime divides the number.  In this case, the first exponent we obtained is 2, so in fact <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is divisible by the square of a prime.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1239" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Combining these steps, we write a procedure, <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">HasPrimeSquare</Font>, that, given <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>, returns true if <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is divisible by the square of a prime and false if not.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1240" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">HasPrimeSquare := proc(n::posint)
  local c, facts, powers, x, e;
  c := binomial(2*n,n);
  facts := ifactors(c)[2];
  powers := seq(x[2],x=facts);
  for e in powers do
    if e &gt;= 2 then
      return true;
    end if;
  end do;
  return false;
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1242" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Now we write a second routine that will test the values of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> from 1 to a maximum.  The procedure prints a message whenever it finds an <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEibkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> for which <Font executable="false" style="Maple Input">HasPrimeSquare</Font> returns false.  It also prints a message when it concludes.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1243" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">CheckPrimeSquare := proc(m::posint)
  local n;
  for n from 1 to m do
    if not HasPrimeSquare(n) then
      print(&quot;Found counterexample: &quot;,n);
    end if;
  end do;
  print(&quot;finished&quot;);
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
